            <ArticleTitle>Degenerative disc disease in childhood and adolescence.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>70-2</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Degenerative disk disease (DDD) is a common cause of low back pain and leg pain in children and infants. DDD is often unrecognized and under-diagnosed. This paper presents six cases of DDD in children and discusses the clinical presentation and pathophysiology of DDD.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
